---
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Herdr backend — sum" active="herdr">
  <div class="doc">
    <h1 style="margin:0 0 16px">Herdr backend</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Herdr owns processes and worktrees. Pane identity, env start and stop,
      native event delivery, and native metadata.
    </p>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2>Pane identity</h2>
      <p>
        Herdr 0.9.0 pane and agent objects carry a <code>terminal_id</code> and,
        when an official integration reports it, an <code>agent_session</code>.
        sum judges a recorded address against those fields. It invents no
        generation field, and a socket path or a bare pid is never identity.
      </p>
      <div class="kv" style="grid-template-columns:1fr">
        <div class="v">
          A <code>server stop</code> and restart restores the saved layout under
          the same pane IDs, with a new terminal_id and a new shell.
        </div>
        <div class="v" style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">
          A <code>kill -9</code> restart restores only what was saved; a later
          pane can receive a freed ID.
        </div>
        <div class="v">
          A live handoff keeps pane IDs and the shell process, and still issues
          a new terminal_id.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2>Environments</h2>
      <CodeBlock>
        <div>./bin/sumctl env discover TASK_ID        <span style="color:var(--muted)"># declared dev commands from mise/package/Makefile/justfile/Procfile/compose/Dockerfile/devcontainer</span></div>
        <div>./bin/sumctl env record TASK_ID --url http://127.0.0.1:PORT [--log PATH | --pane ID | --container ID]</div>
        <div>./bin/sumctl env inspect TASK_ID         <span style="color:var(--muted)"># re-observe once: stale URLs, configuration drift, missing logs</span></div>
        <div>./bin/sumctl env start TASK_ID --command NAME [--url ... | --match TEXT] [--log PATH] [--timeout S]</div>
        <div>./bin/sumctl env stop TASK_ID [--service ID]</div>
      </CodeBlock>
      <p style="margin:14px 0 0">
        <code>env start</code> launches one command the repository declares in a
        pane split under the worker pane inside the checkout. A timeout is an
        explicit failed state, never a retry or restart. <code>env stop</code>
        re-proves that identity, sends exactly one ctrl+c through Herdr, waits a
        bound for exit, verifies the port is released, and closes only the pane
        sum created. Environments started by hand are never stop targets.
        Credentials in URLs, labels, or paths are refused.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2>Native event delivery (optional)</h2>
      <CodeBlock>
        <div>./bin/sumctl hook enable      <span style="color:var(--muted)"># coordinator only; writes a Herdr plugin manifest under .sum/hook/plugin/ and links it live</span></div>
        <div>./bin/sumctl hook status</div>
        <div>./bin/sumctl hook disable     <span style="color:var(--muted)"># or --unlink</span></div>
      </CodeBlock>
      <p style="margin:14px 0 0">
        On a recorded pane going idle/done, the handler re-observes the pane and
        runs one bounded pump toward that recipient: pending questions, reports,
        answers, and requested brief revisions are delivered at the boundary
        instead of waiting for the next rundown. A recorded worker seen blocked,
        idle with nothing owed, exited, or closed produces an <strong
          >attention</strong
        > record on the task. It is evidence, not a question, a result, a quota
        diagnosis, or permission to approve anything. Disabled, degraded, or
        crashing, the handler changes nothing about ask/report, init, bind, and
        pump.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2>Native metadata (optional)</h2>
      <CodeBlock>
        <div>./bin/sumctl metadata enable</div>
        <div>./bin/sumctl metadata sync [--force]</div>
        <div>./bin/sumctl metadata status</div>
        <div>./bin/sumctl metadata inbox [--grouped] [--open --placement split|overlay|tab|zoomed]</div>
        <div>./bin/sumctl metadata disable</div>
      </CodeBlock>
      <p style="margin:14px 0 12px">
        sum task state projected as namespaced <code>sum_*</code> tokens on the
        endpoints sum owns, rendered by sidebar rows the user chooses to add.
        Task panes carry sum_state, sum_pipeline, sum_task, sum_repo, sum_rev,
        and sum_pr; the coordinator pane carries sum_inbox and sum_tasks. Panes
        this installation never recorded are never touched.
      </p>
      <div class="chips">
        <span class="chip">needs-decision</span>
        <span class="chip">needs-attention</span>
        <span class="chip">review-ready</span>
        <span class="chip">answer-pending</span>
        <span class="chip">instruction-refresh-pending</span>
        <span class="chip">running</span>
      </div>
      <p style="margin:12px 0 0">
        These labels never prove verification or completion.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <style>
    .sec p {
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
  </style>
</DocsLayout>
